# Laya browser decision completion review

## Implementation and validation

- The change is archived in standard OpenSpec layout with selected design and pseudocode, a scoped `laya-service` delta, completed tasks, and a merged living spec. Strict validation of `openspec/specs/laya-service/spec.md` passed.
- This publication-shape correction changes documentation only; reviewed runtime source is unchanged.
- The public API remains the existing authenticated SystemOne endpoint, with
  English, multilingual, and browser v10s profiles.
- The browser profile pins Laya source
  `fa9a2a7070b1789912a49ae24603bbfb1a78b001` and checkpoint
  `cklxx/laya-browser@adf912be85ff9221ee171551778456b133c1af75/v10s/`.
- After Code Simplifier and a post-pass rerun, network-disabled pinned-image
  checks passed: worker contracts 10/10, router/readiness 15/15, and browser
  format-v3 adapter 4/4.
- A fresh Camofox exact-ref route regression passed 3/3 for Fiction,
  Historical Fiction, and an empty accessible name. Historical model trials
  remain unchanged.

## Measured outcomes

- On ten frozen Books to Scrape category goals, base Laya selected the target
  label in 1/10 and achieved 0/10 exact click-plus-URL outcomes. Browser v10s
  selected the target label in 9/10 and achieved 8/10 exact outcomes. This is
  a single site-specific set, not general browser accuracy.
- Natural 600-second idle expiry terminated all three model workers without
  interrupting requests; the existing API service remained active. Cgroup
  current was 177,356,800 B before model loads, 6,547,693,568 B with all three
  workers loaded, and 182,960,128 B after expiry. Parent RSS returned to its
  258,809,856 B pre-load baseline.
- A post-expiry browser reload preserved the complete 51-choice inventory,
  returned an offered choice without truncation at native 1024/768 context,
  and used 9.607 s to load the worker and 12.025 s end-to-end. This one reload
  is a smoke measurement, not a latency distribution or navigation-accuracy
  sample.

## Open work

The scoped OpenSpec TODO retains Camofox-to-BrowserUse coordinate integration,
the `Childrens` label mismatch, and OmniRoute routing. No credentials, private
hosts, secret paths, or local environment values are included in this public
handoff.
